<title>GREECE: Greek 1M ATHIBOR slips to 11.89 from 11.90pct.</title>
<headline>Greek 1M ATHIBOR slips to 11.89 from 11.90pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Interbank Offered Rate (Athibor) for one month eased to 11.89 from 11.90 percent and the bid rate (Athibid) was unchanged at 11.41 percent.</p>
<p>ATHIBOR</p>
<p> DATE     1-MTH   2-MTH   3-MTH   6-MTH   9-MTH   12-MTH</p>
<p> Mar  24  11.89   11.83   11.76   11.56   11.42   11.33</p>
<p> Mar  21  11.90   11.83   11.77   11.58   11.43   11.35</p>
<p> Mar  20  11.93   11.88   11.79   11.58   11.47   11.38</p>
<p> Mar  19  11.94   11.88   11.80   11.60   11.47   11.39</p>
<p> Mar  18  11.93   11.88   11.79   11.60   11.48   11.39</p>
<p> Mar  17  11.94   11.88   11.80   11.60   11.49   11.39</p>
<p> Mar  07  11.98   11.90   11.80   11.61   11.50   11.44</p>
<p> Mar  06  11.98   11.91   11.80   11.61   11.50   11.44</p>
<p>ATHIBID</p>
<p> Mar  24  11.41   11.35   11.28   11.07   10.93   10.84</p>
<p> Mar  21  11.41   11.36   11.29   11.08   10.95   10.86</p>
<p> Mar  20  11.44   11.39   11.31   11.10   10.99   10.90</p>
<p> Mar  19  11.45   11.39   11.31   11.11   10.99   10.92</p>
<p> Mar  18  11.45   11.39   11.31   11.11   11.00   10.92</p>
<p> Mar  17  11.46   11.39   11.31   11.12   11.01   10.91</p>
<p> Mar  07  11.49   11.42   11.32   11.12   11.02   10.96</p>
<p> Mar  06  11.49   11.42   11.32   11.12   11.02   10.96</p>
<p>Note: ATHIBOR is Greece's official reference rate. It comprises 18 leading state and private banks committed to quoting their rates by 0900 GMT every day. </p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
